{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><i>To live for all eternity is hard. To love for all eternity is even harder.</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">You play as Jonathan Harker, Dracula\u2019s real estate agent, completing work tasks while <strong>exploring the castle, speaking with its inhabitants, and hacking into computers</strong>. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><i>BYTE</i> is a <strong>tactics RPG</strong> that adapts the classic novel <i>Dracula</i>, by Bram Stoker, with an emphasis on the <strong>themes of queerness and technology</strong>.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">An Internet-Age Dracula</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><i>BYTE</i> takes place in <strong>Detroit, Oregon in 1990. Dracula hires Jonathan Harker to help him purchase properties using the help of fax machines, telephones, and the internet. </strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Rapid developments to transportation, communication, and medical technologies lie at the core of <i>Dracula</i>\u2019s horror, and <i><strong>BYTE</strong></i><strong> explores how the novel adapts to a technological revolution still happening today</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><i>BYTE</i>\u2019s story happens in <strong>visual novel scenes</strong>, where Jonathan talks with the other characters and delivers his own intricate internal monologue.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><i><strong>BYTE</strong></i><strong> is all about the clash between 19th-century Gothic and 20th-century technology</strong>, so retaining the literary style of the novel is a core part of the experience.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Jonathan Harker, Hacker</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Combat in <i>BYTE</i> happens when Jonathan needs to <strong>hack into a computer</strong>. Hacking takes the form of <strong>grid-based tactics battles</strong> where Jonathan needs to accomplish tasks rather than directly fight enemies. Tasks can include <strong>collecting data, getting through firewalls, installing software, and more</strong>.</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/2946750?t=1749173914","background_raw":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2946750/page_bg_raw.jpg?t=1749173914","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2946750/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1749173914","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2946750/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1749173914","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Full controller support","id":28},{"description":"Captions available","id":13},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"controller_support":"full","demos":[{"appid":3344860,"description":""}],"detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><i>To live for all eternity is hard. To love for all eternity is even harder.</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">You play as Jonathan Harker, Dracula\u2019s real estate agent, completing work tasks while <strong>exploring the castle, speaking with its inhabitants, and hacking into computers</strong>. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><i>BYTE</i> is a <strong>tactics RPG</strong> that adapts the classic novel <i>Dracula</i>, by Bram Stoker, with an emphasis on the <strong>themes of queerness and technology</strong>.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">An Internet-Age Dracula</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><i>BYTE</i> takes place in <strong>Detroit, Oregon in 1990. Dracula hires Jonathan Harker to help him purchase properties using the help of fax machines, telephones, and the internet. </strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Rapid developments to transportation, communication, and medical technologies lie at the core of <i>Dracula</i>\u2019s horror, and <i><strong>BYTE</strong></i><strong> explores how the novel adapts to a technological revolution still happening today</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><i>BYTE</i>\u2019s story happens in <strong>visual novel scenes</strong>, where Jonathan talks with the other characters and delivers his own intricate internal monologue.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"><i><strong>BYTE</strong></i><strong> is all about the clash between 19th-century Gothic and 20th-century technology</strong>, so retaining the literary style of the novel is a core part of the experience.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\"></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\">Jonathan Harker, Hacker</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\">Combat in <i>BYTE</i> happens when Jonathan needs to <strong>hack into a computer</strong>. Hacking takes the form of <strong>grid-based tactics battles</strong> where Jonathan needs to accomplish tasks rather than directly fight enemies. Tasks can include <strong>collecting data, getting through firewalls, installing software, and more</strong>.</p>","developers":["James Martini"],"genres":[{"description":"Adventure","id":"25"},{"description":"Indie","id":"23"},{"description":"RPG","id":"3"},{"description":"Strategy","id":"2"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2946750/header.jpg?t=1749173914","is_free":false,"linux_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>"},"mac_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"></ul>"},"movies":[{"highlight":true,"id":257016533,"mp4":{"480":"http://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/257016533/movie480.mp4?t=1731776482","max":"http://video.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_trailers/257016533/movie_max.mp4?t=1731776482"},"name":"BYTE Trailer","thumbnail":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/257016